epos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/commits/382b673b2ab4789826526b8aedcaffc8bc390634/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-21T20:46:39Z","email":"matheuskindrazki@gmail.com","name":"Matheus Kindrazki"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-21T20:46:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(shell): lift content above the reading scrim (text no longer dimmed) (#55)\n\nThe reading scrim (ContentScrim, fixed z-2, dark left gradient) was painting\nOVER the route text — the /skills fun-fact quote looked dimmed, ''under a black\nlayer''. Root cause: a prior fix dropped the shell to z-0 (to stop clipping the\nblack-hole explosion), which left the z-2 scrim above the shell content.\n\nRaise the shell to z-index:3 — above the scrim and the grain (both z-2) — so\ntext is on top again. The shell is transparent, so the Pixi canvas (z-0) and\nits explosion still show through and are NOT clipped (overflow:hidden only\nclips the shell''s own children, not the sibling canvas). The scrim stays at\nz-2, below the shell, so it still darkens the photo/black-hole behind the text\nwithout covering it.\n\nVerified headless at 1440 across /skills, /, /sobre, /projetos: quote is\ncrisp white (hit-test = blockquote, not scrim), explosion renders full (not\nclipped), home/sobre scrims still darken their portraits, chrome on top, nav\nworks. tsc + next build clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ceedeaafdde4ee8d1f8771db30708b55a9064603","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/git/trees/ceedeaafdde4ee8d1f8771db30708b55a9064603"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/git/commits/382b673b2ab4789826526b8aedcaffc8bc390634","verification":{"payload":"tree ceedeaafdde4ee8d1f8771db30708b55a9064603\nparent 7ca5f22172b69d1084077e94b800019d011380a7\nauthor Matheus Kindrazki <matheuskindrazki@gmail.com> 1782074799 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782074799 -0300\n\nfix(shell): lift content above the reading scrim (text no longer dimmed) (#55)\n\nThe reading scrim (ContentScrim, fixed z-2, dark left gradient) was painting\nOVER the route text — the /skills fun-fact quote looked dimmed, ''under a black\nlayer''. Root cause: a prior fix dropped the shell to z-0 (to stop clipping the\nblack-hole explosion), which left the z-2 scrim above the shell content.\n\nRaise the shell to z-index:3 — above the scrim and the grain (both z-2) — so\ntext is on top again. The shell is transparent, so the Pixi canvas (z-0) and\nits explosion still show through and are NOT clipped (overflow:hidden only\nclips the shell''s own children, not the sibling canvas). The scrim stays at\nz-2, below the shell, so it still darkens the photo/black-hole behind the text\nwithout covering it.\n\nVerified headless at 1440 across /skills, /, /sobre, /projetos: quote is\ncrisp white (hit-test = blockquote, not scrim), explosion renders full (not\nclipped), home/sobre scrims still darken their portraits, chrome on top, nav\nworks. tsc + next build clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOE2vCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm3cQADY5r/9GHXILzL01Pm6ErtZK\n+CPwAqwMGHq1CFRTvhPy+P4ZguMghy25G2uvpgLgtWP1Gx9CHR0XDSKoQLVNDVyW\nS/77sXxGgrHuqg417lulysXBd8xbwAKndBwW4p2dI+2W6G+DOcKZ7p4mepO+WWPd\n2DGk8dV6hq6JXFm4CueiuRMISo5eZTuXQzR8MihHTSReyUdJUY6nXSpWmZEhQJB5\nS/hmCInjCboVNWC1CbnY6pY9LAhLPTVjCJWiazxNsitxO/DrYnwW1fUtxFmDholP\ngNTdAZJBDk5Ty/XcfrJ1TtQMXOqkQkI1DNETZJxqGPdUW7K56c57+RGU1h1Qtt7M\nlU4oJCwoBTq0YIZrIqwWRkWdH9Eamwoplc3J