ndrazki/MatheusKindrazki/commit/f541e5856d2b296a46608169ba9409627fdfe4bf","sha":"f541e5856d2b296a46608169ba9409627fdfe4bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/commits/f541e5856d2b296a46608169ba9409627fdfe4bf"}],"sha":"7ca5f22172b69d1084077e94b800019d011380a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/commits/7ca5f22172b69d1084077e94b800019d011380a7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36010251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/MatheusKindrazki","id":36010251,"login":"MatheusKindrazki","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDEwMjUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/commits/f541e5856d2b296a46608169ba9409627fdfe4bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-21T18:13:51Z","email":"matheuskindrazki@gmail.com","name":"Matheus Kindrazki"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-21T18:13:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(skills): scroll-driven black-hole video — DJ → piano → rubber (#53)\n\nTwo new fun-fact sections after the DJ one, each swapping the black-hole\nclip as it scrolls to the viewport center:\n- Piano: ''The piano is my favorite instrument — and, modesty aside, I play\n  it well.'' → kindra-piano.mp4\n- Rubber: ''Turns out I also know how to make rubber — some skills don''t fit\n  in a repo.'' → kindra-borracha.mp4\n\nVideos transcoded from the source clips to web h264 + downscaled (piano\n15MB→513KB, rubber 8.8MB→335KB; the originals were mpeg4, which browsers\ncan''t play).\n\nMechanics:\n- An IntersectionObserver per fun-fact fires when the section crosses the\n  vertical middle (threshold 0, rootMargin -45%/-45%). NOTE: the obvious\n   is unreachable here — ~900px sections in a -25% root cap at\n  ~0.47 — so the center-band approach is used instead.\n- BlackHoleLayer gains a fast media-swap: when only  changes (same\n  formation, hole already formed) it swaps the clip in place instead of\n  re-running the ~7.6s collapse — instant, no re-fetch.\n- Section now forwards a ref (needed to observe each section).\n\nVerified headless at 1440: all 3 sections show their correct distinct video,\neach playing, swap is instant. tsc + next build clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cfe43356d1b228e920b46b38f9a32c20f5c50cd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/git/trees/cfe43356d1b228e920b46b38f9a32c20f5c50cd6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/git/commits/f541e5856d2b296a46608169ba9409627fdfe4bf","verification":{"payload":"tree cfe43356d1b228e920b46b38f9a32c20f5c50cd6\nparent aae7bcf1a3aa226f69af8461d3ccd72437593a7c\nauthor Matheus Kindrazki <matheuskindrazki@gmail.com> 1782065631 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782065631 -0300\n\nfeat(skills): scroll-driven black-hole video — DJ → piano → rubber (#53)\n\nTwo new fun-fact sections after the DJ one, each swapping the black-hole\nclip as it scrolls to the viewport center:\n- Piano: ''The piano is my favorite instrument — and, modesty aside, I play\n  it well.'' → kindra-piano.mp4\n- Rubber: ''Turns out I also know how to make rubber — some skills don''t fit\n  in a repo.'' → kindra-borracha.mp4\n\nVideos transcoded from the source clips to web h264 + downscaled (piano\n15MB→513KB, rubber 8.8MB→335KB; the originals were mpeg4, which browsers\ncan''t play).\n\nMechanics:\n- An IntersectionObserver per fun-fact fires when the section crosses the\n  vertical middle (threshold 0, rootMargin -45%/-45%). NOTE: the obvious\n   is unreachable here — ~900px sections in a -25% root cap at\n  ~0.47 — so the center-band approach is used instead.\n- BlackHoleLayer gains a fast media-swap: when only  changes (same\n  formation, hole already formed) it swaps the clip in place instead of\n  re-running the ~7.6s collapse — instant, no re-fetch.\n- Section now forwards a ref (needed to observe each section).\n\nVerified headless at 1440: all 3 sections show their correct distinct video,\neach playing, swap is instant. tsc + next build clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOCnfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoHYQAFS7yitqClUs9PcDu7RYowW8\nkWtyPgdJSDBolyEbCZRMeTv/vtXdxLfXQkzxrYOPhjThLlQwJMgdR7wUhloqZLw1\nclS4U32clWVed7I+SyqajOrNc/FqohaRJ/q2NRkmiu4YKq+2rx17n6FNmVC8tIbO\nbTu9bh1bj+wW0Pkey/bPp85XucdPt3Qpftn5UH8aO/KcFDuoeQQVJO4qPDydmd4X\nyIPQs9nZ9KT5Pla+e4C8bfU915QLqeZt6cPHowUhcaLNidiiz4emLRXLMA8wNCgB\nug3hD3IyLzTgg4FxRy76CUH64Km1mi4N1x7jn9UE36I3qq2OUMq84CiH79E6a1ES\nH4cprcwBke2re/gastI/+J5ALT/TJoSOW89wigLoFsxgFRZquJTe03s+gXFxKACN\nR9wKBPPrOJtmQp9TJZ4URSZbTSF3mWOmvmnb60FCAqGxVtUHo3d1ta0503hW6qv0\nInRcv0W00CvNAyXrsFELyk4hOhDdk8UIeXENFmMT6FEog3OiqUY22gz6zd+e1xgs\n69f4SNQ5obTR/LZaazAMEFJ+ioySRFWfg46RWoQBS2ZZaVc4MJF4nAInDgB1mqzQ\npKa0EgBhZfxiVaHAYrEnCT0o2UldRoZEKNDhg5Ck+cXZ443dQiCvrJnMl4mDAnrP\ny7qYQ2lAK9dmrcGjA9eu\n=XJKX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-21T18:13:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/commit/f541e5856d2b296a46608169ba9409627fdfe4bf","node_id":"C_kwDOEKA_0toAKGY1NDFlNTg1NmQyYjI5NmE0NjYwODE2OWJhOTQwOTYyN2ZkZmU0YmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/commit/aae7bcf1a3aa226f69af8461d3ccd72437593a7c","sha":"aae7bcf1a3aa226f69af8461d3ccd72437593a7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/commits/aae7bcf1a3aa226f69af8461d3ccd72437593a7c"}],"sha":"f541e5856d2b296a46608169ba9409627fdfe4bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/commits/f541e5856d2b296a46608169ba9409627fdfe4bf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36010251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/MatheusKindrazki","id":36010251,"login":"MatheusKindrazki","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDEwMjUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/commits/aae7bcf1a3aa226f69af8461d3ccd72437593a7c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-21T16:29:29Z","email":"matheuskindrazki@gmail.com","name":"Matheus Kindrazki"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-21T16:29:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(shell): stop content from clipping the Pixi explosion (z-index) (#52)\n\nThe shell was z-index:10 — above the fixed Pixi background canvas (z-0) — so\nthe centered 1280px content box visually clipped the black-hole explosion as\nits rings expanded past the box (most visible on /skills entry). Drop the\nshell to z-index:0 (same plane as the canvas, transparent, so nothing is\nclipped) and lift the inner .scroll content to z-index:1 (still above the\nbackground, readable). Chrome (z-30) and the explode/transition layers stay\nabove content within the shell''s context.\n\nVerified headless at 1440 across /, /skills, /projetos, /sobre: explosion\nrenders as full concentric rings (no rectangular clip), no route lost its\nbackground, text stays readable, chrome stays on top, nav works. build clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9fdc9674a57760a4d0cf95d96bf3896e70c24f70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/git/trees/9fdc9674a57760a4d0cf95d96bf3896e70c24f70"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/git/commits/aae7bcf1a3aa226f69af8461d3ccd72437593a7c","verification":{"payload":"tree 9fdc9674a57760a4d0cf95d96bf3896e70c24f70\nparent 72d6ab03fc5cfa6fc12bb8df66d3b4759cf00d14\nauthor Matheus Kindrazki <matheuskindrazki@gmail.com> 1782059369 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782059369 -0300\n\nfix(shell): stop content from clipping the Pixi explosion (z-index) (#52)\n\nThe shell was z-index:10 — above the fixed Pixi background canvas (z-0) — so\nthe centered 1280px content box visually clipped the black-hole explosion as\nits rings expanded past the box (most visible on /skills entry). Drop the\nshell to z-index:0 (same plane as the canvas, transparent, so nothing is\nclipped) and lift the inner .scroll content to z-index:1 (still above the\nbackground, readable). Chrome (z-30) and the explode/transition layers stay\nabove content within the shell''s context.\n\nVerified headless at 1440 across /, /skills, /projetos, /sobre: explosion\nrenders as full concentric rings (no rectangular clip), no route lost its\nbackground, text stays readable, chrome stays on top, nav works. build clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOBFpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuCQQAK6cL1yUIQlm+xWgm2ZuuJVw\npAs9bk7wUe6+54X/QDrkNI5hOO044QKywkdMnKtaviu1snLsk2mYy1cFWBlw2d5+\nQA4tneXIGx61TddCbrV/7bbFECV3DcQujvPOebdFtjUYroZcIgU+idwg2MB/4y1S\nhJ7ID2n+OgVZl3LdYt/4Yd29lqQ3qguS63C2YJ/ogD8qNrWs+8W/SvM8aVVJT4cV\np8W8+6jJjTFKiCGKB2QWMe6T4m4iiutlaQTJJQBqp5vWrS0u3j2PuAHnGOnXXqX8\n2IPj2Is3+Gckk2BfPEwTglXGw29y9eC+A4f5dy/4xNa+/HHQnkjhYuXryBuEH7AA\n3/rEco7BN42lxlKmcf76bCyJcdm1sms1H7i+G0jf2mqjJAxhrX31rcoEKYizk6W8\nUiINyoUICbgUt0n5ubjlSGp3Wm2bnAqXsv7Zy65usUetqGf6buNhHPpL1I3UUomA\nHtRqWJOfrhu5olama5vRLV/wVdeaqXJkaVgbW+IsPmc9kyahFXNbKZ+xctiMnKsB\n2z8remGo2ReNxUj/9YepKwrCxCL9tt437d8MjYsLo