MatheusKindrazki/commits/314d23d128669bd1cdaf61cab44ac1a2addec6ff"}],"sha":"541b5e70f83d8cd5a0b580361f30e23d3c22903f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/commits/541b5e70f83d8cd5a0b580361f30e23d3c22903f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36010251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/MatheusKindrazki","id":36010251,"login":"MatheusKindrazki","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDEwMjUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/commits/314d23d128669bd1cdaf61cab44ac1a2addec6ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-21T15:41:56Z","email":"matheuskindrazki@gmail.com","name":"Matheus Kindrazki"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-21T15:41:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(content): correct Lugui & Arco, add FastShared/Lavra/ScreenshotDetox (#49)\n\n* fix(content): correct Lugui (real-estate AI) + Arco AI tenure & essay-vision project\n\nTwo factual corrections:\n- Lugui.ai: it''s AI infrastructure for the REAL-ESTATE market (''the\n  intelligence of your agency, inside WhatsApp'' — conversational agents +\n  RAG for realtors), NOT an education/tutoring platform. Fixed the project\n  dossier, nowNote, tags, profile description, and the /sobre timeline.\n- Arco Educação: tenure was 2020→2025/26 (~6 years), not 2020-2024. Matheus\n  consolidated as Principal Engineer of AI there and worked on applied-AI\n  projects. Replaced the generic ''AI Education Tools'' card with the real\n  last delivery — the ENEM AI essay-correction platform, where he led the\n  core pipeline and OWNED the computer-vision model that reads handwritten\n  essays (OCR/HTR). Updated the platform card date + role and the timeline.\nFacts sourced from the user + Jarvis memory + lugui.ai.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(projetos): add FastShared, Lavra, ScreenshotDetox + fix 15-node atlas spacing\n\nThree new side products (own builds, 2026, privacy-first / on-device):\n- FastShared: ephemeral Apple-native file sharing + agent CLI (fastsha.red).\n- Lavra: offline macOS audio→text on Apple Silicon (WhisperKit + Foundation\n  Models), strong PT-BR / WhatsApp audio.\n- ScreenshotDetox: on-device iOS screenshot triage (Vision OCR + local\n  classifier). Shown as ''Detox'' on the atlas node (full name in the dossier).\n\nThe atlas now carries 15 bodies, so the placement was retuned to keep labels\nfrom colliding: widened the side ring arc (120°→210°), added shell\nalternation on the side + current rings so same-year cohorts don''t stack on\none radius, and capped node-label text at 92px. Verified headless (ink-rect\nmeasurement, not container boxes) at 1440 + 1280: zero text overlaps between\nnodes, nothing clipped. tsc + next build clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e6d703d1020a7bd9bf54953420b740e2f6639ac5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/git/trees/e6d703d1020a7bd9bf54953420b740e2f6639ac5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/git/commits/314d23d128669bd1cdaf61cab44ac1a2addec6ff","verification":{"payload":"tree e6d703d1020a7bd9bf54953420b740e2f6639ac5\nparent 371c08167a00727cd61bb3387cc332cc0e13e6da\nauthor Matheus Kindrazki <matheuskindrazki@gmail.com> 1782056516 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782056516 -0300\n\nfix(content): correct Lugui & Arco, add FastShared/Lavra/ScreenshotDetox (#49)\n\n* fix(content): correct Lugui (real-estate AI) + Arco AI tenure & essay-vision project\n\nTwo factual corrections:\n- Lugui.ai: it''s AI infrastructure for the REAL-ESTATE market (''the\n  intelligence of your agency, inside WhatsApp'' — conversational agents +\n  RAG for realtors), NOT an education/tutoring platform. Fixed the project\n  dossier, nowNote, tags, profile description, and the /sobre timeline.\n- Arco Educação: tenure was 2020→2025/26 (~6 years), not 2020-2024. Matheus\n  consolidated as Principal Engineer of AI there and worked on applied-AI\n  projects. Replaced the generic ''AI Education Tools'' card with the real\n  last delivery — the ENEM AI essay-correction platform, where he led the\n  core pipeline and OWNED the computer-vision model that reads handwritten\n  essays (OCR/HTR). Updated the platform card date + role and the timeline.\nFacts sourced from the user + Jarvis memory + lugui.ai.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(projetos): add FastShared, Lavra, ScreenshotDetox + fix 15-node atlas spacing\n\nThree new side products (own builds, 2026, privacy-first / on-device):\n- FastShared: ephemeral Apple-native file sharing + agent CLI (fastsha.red).\n- Lavra: offline macOS audio→text on Apple Silicon (WhisperKit + Foundation\n  Models), strong PT-BR / WhatsApp audio.\n- ScreenshotDetox: on-device iOS screenshot triage (Vision OCR + local\n  classifier). Shown as ''Detox'' on the atlas node (full name in the dossier).\n\nThe atlas now carries 15 bodies, so the placement was retuned to keep labels\nfrom colliding: widened the side ring arc (120°→210°), added shell\nalternation on the side + current rings so same-year cohorts don''t stack on\none radius, and capped node-label text at 92px. Verified headless (ink-rect\nmeasurement, not container boxes) at 1440 + 1280: zero text overlaps between\nnodes, nothing clipped. tsc + next build clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOAZECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALogQAKUhrisXQPtp5sYHXnsejhIM\nEl+fCSfDUBF/J1kVeyJFRmEtUSIy7RoiU4isE2GpiZAt0PGabTA8XJkdWtEbshT8\nKwxxn7MACZ3d9iut3KMDzQ6u7tsh6SxAlPAaTgRiRMTijEnhMK7/wYeZyQbwB4Sd\n3jg4aFpoLQXHxZi3xOPozFd3wJEDfZgAfVe+sbKGVbAmfK12SnpnndUKLbqGWCSF\nvvLFGlokQrMCc92h8Nfh6HnTs1Kq83TRT/vG+Elv0oCc7fEPlQ2bvZd88KVsIt6k\nKsbUv4c6KXvvPq9HhzfcBHNxBtYhxlXkhk2kItqYXVruZ2CHJ3NIqmNmuGl0O3oh\nZhfDHXzaFxHh+sKTK8cgRHZTZhGUumHSrdAxt7g1nJUxofs6LcGhoFs8WHux5R8K\nzZjNVUR+77sABdIu6WnJq19KaoesbWozp46NtGhBi8maZhbbI62KYFkZlhJi2kuL\nxctCNaQV93uhgbXh0PkCCr8qkayPergM6J1g9Jw1Wf9XGCs1r8Cjz0qn2VTJI/ge\nMIKin2Aioa3ZahjCooFgk1A59nY8/CBVzVsZMnwHyGuMP25NjkAlM3XpI38UvKLg\nsQlFxwGJ0n35RZO/VZW1OB423zpOoPQJ5MAvhwZY62eKqggzYPsG6oLBTrom39Sj\nhExm7vzIsbhvT3PmT4JS\n=i2o5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-21T15:41:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/commit/314d23d128669bd1cdaf61cab44ac1a2addec6ff","node_id":"C_kwDOEKA_0toAKDMxNGQyM2QxMjg2NjliZDFjZGFmNjFjYWI0NGFjMWEyYWRkZWM2ZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/commit/371c08167a00727cd61bb3387cc332cc0e13e6da","sha":"371c08167a00727cd61bb3387cc332cc0e13e6da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/commits/371c08167a00727cd61bb3387cc332cc0e13e6da"}],"sha":"314d23d128669bd1cdaf61cab44ac1a2addec6ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/commits/314d23d128669bd1cdaf61cab44ac1a2addec6ff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36010251?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/MatheusKindrazki","id":36010251,"login":"MatheusKindrazki","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDEwMjUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/commits/371c08167a00727cd61bb3387cc332cc0e13e6da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-18T14:52:25Z","email":"matheuskindrazki@gmail.com","name":"Matheus Kindrazki"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-18T14:52:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"security: disconnect public chat from the personal Jarvis backend (#48)\n\nCRITICAL: the public portfolio chat proxied every anonymous visitor message\nstraight to the owner''s personal Jarvis (platform:''api''), which the backend\ntreats as the owner — exposing private context (profile, agenda, memory,\ndocuments) AND executing actions (observed creating tasks). Any stranger\ncould read personal data and mutate the owner''s system.\n\nContain it now: /api/ask no longer calls Jarvis. It validates input and\nreturns a fixed ''offline for visitors — reach me via contact'' message. The\nproxy path is gated behind an explicit JARVIS_PUBLIC_MODE=''enabled'' opt-in\n(setting the key alone is no longer enough) and, when re-enabled, sends\nplatform:''public'' + mode:''public_readonly'' + allow_actions:false — but the\nbackend MUST enforce a hardened read-only no-personal-data mode before that\nenv is ever flipped.\n\nUI made honest: chat status ''private assistant · offline'' (was ''knowledge\ngraph · active'' with a live green dot); intro explains it''s private and\npoints to contact; starter-prompt chips removed; content.ts no longer claims\na ''live Jarvis instance answers questions right here''.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"185bbaf7bf35218769b2b6cd55b8d365ad32018c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/git/trees/185bbaf7bf35218769b2b6cd55b8d365ad32018c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/git/commits/371c08167a00727cd61bb3387cc332cc0e13e6da","verification":{"payload":"tree 185bbaf7bf35218769b2b6cd55b8d365ad32018c\nparent 6ba13f3dc24017b04daa8a0df3e96c65cbe0298a\nauthor Matheus Kindrazki <matheuskindrazki@gmail.com> 1781794345 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781794345 -0300\n\nsecurity: disconnect public chat from the personal Jarvis backend (#48)\n\nCRITICAL: the public portfolio chat proxied every anonymous visitor message\nstraight to the owner''s personal Jarvis (platform:''api''), which the backend\ntreats as the owner — exposing private context (profile, agenda, memory,\ndocuments) AND executing actions (observed creating tasks). Any stranger\ncould read personal data and mutate the owner''s system.\n\nContain it now: /api/ask no longer calls Jarvis. It validates input and\nreturns a fixed ''offline for visitors — reach me via contact'' message. The\nproxy path is gated behind an explicit JARVIS_PUBLIC_MODE=''enabled'' opt-in\n(setting the key alone is no longer enough) and, when re-enabled, sends\nplatform:''public'' + mode:''public_readonly'' + allow_actions:false — but the\nbackend MUST enforce a hardened read-only no-personal-data mode before that\nenv is ever flipped.\n\nUI made honest: chat status ''private assistant · offline'' (was ''knowledge\ngraph · active'' with a live green dot); intro explains it''s private and\npoints to contact; starter-prompt chips removed; content.ts no longer claims\na ''live Jarvis instance answers questions right here''.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNAYpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7+cQACGzJZTgphIuQV+skRxkoTWV\nKl/Yq5bj56imWhVqmqSMJrazc+X75hOgrQtFsWL1ywp/GX9tnzrATWnr7aRcq9Ry\nWOckxIoTDWf+gaB72sYwp8ZNmZd6bqK9D0JGjmOpJvXZlvlgJpU78KlL5FFkuARu\nkb3YefK0to11ZP77QSZYAfErifh4W7S0hhnQxV7/KEczB5uPLx+yi9eyPFlSKWCa\nebDRsyHLoYgHfD7RtTMH2aYpy+aUm05RUenaRG33+1jdJt1D0HxqNOmGAkM