/MatheusKindrazki/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatheusKindrazki","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/commits/7ea971e9b354903e27ef86eb7a6f637e2a24328c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T16:57:55Z","email":"matheuskindrazki@gmail.com","name":"Matheus Kindrazki"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T16:57:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(skills): boomerang loop for the black-hole video (#45)\n\nThe DJ clip now plays forward, glides back in reverse, and repeats as one\ncontinuous take — the sense of continuity instead of a hard restart cut.\nPre-rendered with ffmpeg (forward + reverse concatenated, audio stripped)\nso the native <video loop> handles it with zero runtime cost — h264 can''t\nreliably seek backwards, so doing it in a pre-built clip is smoother than\ndriving currentTime by rAF. The seam is frame-matched (last frame ≈ first,\nmean diff 3.9/255) for a seamless restart. New clip is lighter than the old\none (1.9MB vs 2.6MB); removed the now-unused kindra-skills.mp4.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"59005adee9e736c0356974339b34e7158fa144b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/git/trees/59005adee9e736c0356974339b34e7158fa144b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatheusKindrazki/MatheusKindrazki/git/commits/7ea971e9b354903e27ef86eb7a6f637e2a24328c","verification":{"payload":"tree 59005adee9e736c0356974339b34e7158fa144b4\nparent 2c0bc7542140e5981e12cf6f9e048724c446dc88\nauthor Matheus Kindrazki <matheuskindrazki@gmail.com> 1781456275 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781456275 -0300\n\nfeat(skills): boomerang loop for the black-hole video (#45)\n\nThe DJ clip now plays forward, glides back in reverse, and repeats as one\ncontinuous take — the sense of continuity instead of a hard restart cut.\nPre-rendered with ffmpeg (forward + reverse concatenated, audio stripped)\nso the native <video loop> handles it with zero runtime cost — h264 can''t\nreliably seek backwards, so doing it in a pre-built clip is smoother than\ndriving currentTime by rAF. The seam is frame-matched (last frame ≈ first,\nmean diff 3.9/255) for a seamless restart. New clip is lighter than the old\none (1.9MB vs 2.6MB); removed the now-unused kindra-skills.mp4.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLt2TCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIuEQAK2WhFMRsITK4VsbpRTkxCG4\noEoKIccnfIQESHjfvIQ0a8PWzuoMuhbbr90RtFkFLvZSI5tY8h6SPnjs1F0YanwD\nOnsXvT9+vRFkWWIPwgKGmpbwfSGDob1//53nEJ3n6BKPcuB90a+yPA8O3/5vW2zL\n9jY5qbky/CWURhFyK9FaW+o5A2IurZA6Px8s4WmZs4g/PpkZnQBjCVZSnw29VtKy\nLqFj+gYPFSOneXnsbpHo+t9s7low9a5YcI72cBaRMDku5ocA6Cz/1B/myL19438j\nYfOaWVSJHsCDGv+CJVN9gd+FTzh6w0fuNsRJwNc6zihBox30dnpKG4hCosWSjyB3\nhv0hc8WHeumZ0BqnKeDWDBOcsb+e4ZjXkJ0iwqUqBmbT26g5XPdB/JXp1EtNeJ9a\ncyLLzYRgY3boKOl7XVrSbjvgY94G5ceCrhEafHeYE6308kqNwrx8QjHs//a6HO21\npGSctYbdr+1nVC92IjB8XirZVwV3fLMwQdCPOtlc3t6PX/0zNTHGjzH+FOafMndg\nPlyMuJKNKzpn+Rq/AERwsTvCg30rkw5igExjgnYRsdd0vLrTdLBrlIr2OWF43+6n\n/HhKWPJeE6CzQTuHl/KLR1Ckjnrne5duryVMEf35BL3m0iJ1BQsi/l7uS5V1Spvi\npEvplc/czSt7dr/4b7aY\n=Gpu5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-14T16:57:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.co