","committedDate":"2026-09-12T19:12:48Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T17:31:26.473Z","repositoryId":285295187,"sha":"eb0a378062fe34cb624adc9097d9f4b2706dfc4f"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"sanbales","providerType":"User"},"email":"sanbales@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Santiago Balestrini-Robinson"},"authoredDate":"2026-09-12T17:55:18Z","committedDate":"2026-09-12T17:55:18Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T17:31:26.473Z","repositoryId":285295187,"sha":"c5ed9d0048e7c85f2b4cc9692096bfc0d333800b"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"sanbales","providerType":"User"},"email":"sanbales@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Santiago Balestrini-Robinson"},"authoredDate":"2026-09-12T14:52:15Z","committedDate":"2026-09-12T14:52:15Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T17:31:26.473Z","repositoryId":285295187,"sha":"3bceadfe9b8c3e596226b935541bc571795f94d6"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"sanbales","providerType":"User"},"email":"sanbales@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Santiago Balestrini-Robinson"},"authoredDate":"2026-09-07T16:03:21Z","committedDate":"2026-09-07T16:03:21Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T17:31:26.473Z","repositoryId":285295187,"sha":"df44f387aa5539f8b2a8f1e4b9375568803919c1"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"nrbgt","providerType":"User"},"email":"nicholas.bollweg@gtri.gatech.edu","name":"Nicholas Bollweg"},"authoredDate":"2026-09-02T00:32:27Z","committedDate":"2026-09-02T00:32:27Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T17:31:26.473Z","repositoryId":285295187,"sha":"8a8ef9e0c48ea3dffea326ba0839a585ec4797bb"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T17:31:26.473Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6493354?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dfreeman06","id":6493354,"login":"dfreeman06","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0OTMzNTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commits/2a36eb069ee5ac0711427cac195c2a1a6f5f2bd8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T13:10:49Z","email":"freeman.dane@gmail.com","name":"dfreeman06"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T13:10:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Log routine id fixes at debug, not warning (#189)\n\n* Log routine id fixes at debug, not warning\n\nValidationPipe assigns ids to id-less elements on every diagram built\nfrom them, which is normal since the 2.1.3 id work. Logging each one as\na warning wrote to the kernel''s stderr, and that output is the last\nthing before the intermittent kernel stall captured in #177: ipykernel''s\nfd-capture thread was stuck creating an IOPub event-pipe socket while\nforwarding it. Debug level removes ipyelk''s trigger; the stall itself is\nlikely upstream and stays tracked in #177.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Pin the id-fix log level; drop the unfounded #177 link\n\nReview showed the \"fixing N ids\" warning cannot have triggered the #177\nkernel stall: ipykernel routes logger output to a copy of the raw stderr\nfd, never through the fd-capture thread the stack dump appeared to show\nstuck, and that \"stuck\" frame is the watchdog''s own dump being forwarded.\nThe level change stays as plain noise reduction; the CHANGELOG now says\nonly that, and a test pins the message at debug.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dane <dane@Mac-Box.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Dane <freeman.dane.mallory@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"9be21efe789ecda6e15fcba3cf0af6c1df33e268","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/git/trees/9be21efe789ecda6e15fcba3cf0af6c1df33e268"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/git/commits/2a36eb069ee5ac0711427cac195c2a1a6f5f2bd8","verification":{"payload":"tree 9be21efe789ecda6e15fcba3cf0af6c1df33e268\nparent 4c923de60343ed09aa537ad6fe955f4ea46b85fd\nauthor dfreeman06 <freeman.dane@gmail.com> 1791465049 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791465049 -0400\n\nLog routine id fixes at debug, not warning (#189)\n\n* Log routine id fixes at debug, not warning\n\nValidationPipe assigns ids to id-less elements on every diagram built\nfrom them, which is normal since the 2.1.3 id work. Logging each one as\na warning wrote to the kernel''s stderr, and that output is the last\nthing before the intermittent kernel stall captured in #177: ipykernel''s\nfd-capture thread was stuck creating an IOPub event-pipe socket while\nforwarding it. Debug level removes ipyelk''s trigger; the stall itself is\nlikely upstream and stays tracked in #177.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Pin the id-fix log level; drop the unfounded #177 link\n\nReview showed the \"fixing N ids\" warning cannot have triggered the #177\nkernel stall: ipykernel routes logger output to a copy of the raw stderr\nfd, never through the fd-capture thread the stack dump appeared to show\nstuck, and that \"stuck\" frame is the watchdog''s own dump being forwarded.\nThe level change stays as plain noise reduction; the CHANGELOG now says\nonly that, and a test pins the message at debug.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dane <dane@Mac-Box.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Dane <freeman.dane.mallory@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx5ZZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0eEQAA9xXkfg2svuX811/9mO+wwn\npbrz7ER2qRaDdcuExQwOpJI7TJIVhKVePfOeCH44D4PflsfADEkRzl/C32dFGFWc\nsa4QPDu5o0aC4fkGL9V9sIqjvKoLVvFrNLvsk714+jFzhDRreyvuXhwsywyKe/Dn\nFnNkrIFt9FiA5i6bvTW7atze0RTn/DjpBcDwlCdbkJzjb4h6LE249BKDVTXqfmrv\n1yegRsxj98vs4usHAuVPn1jlNqCdEZMhD3ZbZY/9Gml8DadVPIoVzLNcMG/89Uj9\nIyEY1LH6hjtRTn3eaZglPjJ7utTItNMBIAEUfF3LyqjlEduNruS/1bBolzVzCVXL\nNOS49mkP9/J0eTz/4eSqDxNpCXE1gHJqFtYEoV1Dw7HsHGUYiDgFj+7Asir9+kYx\ngd+TkoSanzHzzXrBukMb/PSUIyhwFCpUkcMhR5CIVPQpNjEljY/6og6t+4UwMSn7\ntFtIUyYqreCNvt5qJVzHf1ekVXk75dAFY1qPgVts0qTJr6MAw7/Dv3q2qCKZFcgJ\n6WsBG/ekG86BtBcV8AXuu192J+c3nD2RM1wTDmbFbbK4HqmMdfM2Tl30Ocx2wLBE\nZE7AHgGCRgDxE+yY29EAfvlt5wm43rjKOvVFf2aGQPRd/4NKu+gjsnIT1kfOt5a/\nbuzOoQQYxlpgtx+/R3tm\n=RgIx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T13:10:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commit/2a36eb069ee5ac0711427cac195c2a1a6f5f2bd8","node_id":"C_kwDOEQFCU9oAKDJhMzZlYjA2OWVlNWFjMDcxMTQyN2NhYzE5NWMyYTFhNmY1ZjJiZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commit/4c923de60343ed09aa537ad6fe955f4ea46b85fd","sha":"4c923de60343ed09aa537ad6fe955f4ea46b85fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commits/4c923de60343ed09aa537ad6fe955f4ea46b85fd"}],"sha":"2a36eb069ee5ac0711427cac195c2a1a6f5f2bd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commits/2a36eb069ee5ac0711427cac195c2a1a6f5f2bd8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1438114?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanbales/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanbales/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanbales/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanbales/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sanbales","id":1438114,"login":"sanbales","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzgxMTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanbales/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanbales/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanbales/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanbales/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanbales/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanbales","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commits/4c923de60343ed09aa537ad6fe955f4ea46b85fd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T08:58:44Z","email":"sanbales@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Santiago Balestrini-Robinson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T08:58:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Cervidae Tree (#162)\n\n* Add frozen Cervidae tree with species photos and interactive exploration\n\n* Fix Vale findings in the Cervidae example after the rebase\n\nmaster now gates CI on Vale (#185). Accept the taxon and Wikimedia terms,\nspell ''labeled'' the en_US way, and mark the review script''s environment and\noption names as code.\n\n* Make the hidden-port geometry test exercise a projection\n\nA hidden child of the root has no visible ancestor to project its port onto,\nso the test passed with or without the ElementIndex.update guard. Nest the\nhidden child in a visible group: without the guard the hidden port takes the\nslack port''s geometry and the test fails.\n\n* Retry the Fit click in the Cervidae acceptance test\n\nA Fit click right after scrolling the app into view can miss the button: the\ncamera stays at scale(1) and the toggles never come into view (3 of 10 local\nruns). Click Fit again until the toggles are in view (14 of 14 local runs).\n\n* Do not count labels after fitting the Cervidae tree\n\nThe Windows test-oldest job failed all three attempts with labels:0 after the\nfirst collapse (nodes, edges and ports were right). Fit zooms out to about\n0.2, and the label view skips a label unless zoom * label height > 3, so\nwhether labels render at that zoom depends on font metrics. Count labels only\nat the unfitted zoom; after Fit, check nodes, edges and ports.\n\n* Fetch LFS files on ReadTheDocs before building the JupyterLite demo\n\nThe lite build copies examples/ into the demo, and ReadTheDocs does not fetch\nLFS objects: the Cervidae notebook would get the 133-byte LFS pointer, and\nzipfile raises BadZipFile. Install conda-forge''s git-lfs in the RTD\nenvironment and pull the LFS files first (checked on a clone made with\nGIT_LFS_SKIP_SMUDGE=1: the pointer becomes the 41 MB archive).\n\n* Use American spelling in the Cervidae robot test comments\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Santiago [C] Balestrini Robinson <sanbales@amazon.com>","tree":{"sha":"91d47f2a9eaf11d0cf9a1e98026202a7d3053aaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/git/trees/91d47f2a9eaf11d0cf9a1e98026202a7d3053aaf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/git/commits/4c923de60343ed09aa537ad6fe955f4ea46b85fd","verification":{"payload":"tree 91d47f2a9eaf11d0cf9a1e98026202a7d3053aaf\nparent d2f06fe205d8737ced3f00b59ab545cd65044a1d\nauthor Santiago Balestrini-Robinson <sanbales@users.noreply.github.com> 1791449924 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791449924 -0400\n\nCervidae Tree (#162)\n\n* Add frozen Cervidae tree with species photos and interactive exploration\n\n* Fix Vale findings in the Cervidae example after the rebase\n\nmaster now gates CI on Vale (#185). Accept the taxon and Wikimedia terms,\nspell ''labeled'' the en_US way, and mark the review script''s environment and\noption names as code.\n\n* Make the hidden-port geometry test exercise a projection\n\nA hidden child of the root has no visible ancestor to project its port onto,\nso the test passed with or without the ElementIndex.update guard. Nest the\nhidden child in a visible group: without the guard the hidden port takes the\nslack port''s geometry and the test fails.\n\n* Retry the Fit click in the Cervidae acceptance test\n\nA Fit click right after scrolling the app into view can miss the button: the\ncamera stays at scale(1) and the toggles never come into view (3 of 10 local\nruns). Click Fit again until the toggles are in view (14 of 14 local runs).\n\n* Do not count labels after fitting the Cervidae tree\n\nThe Windows test-oldest job failed all three attempts with labels:0 after the\nfirst collapse (nodes, edges and ports were right). Fit zooms out to about\n0.2, and the label view skips a label unless zoom * label height > 3, so\nwhether labels render at that zoom depends on font metrics. Count labels only\nat the unfitted zoom; after Fit, check nodes, edges and ports.\n\n* Fetch LFS files on ReadTheDocs before building the JupyterLite demo\n\nThe lite build copies examples/ into the demo, and ReadTheDocs does not fetch\nLFS objects: the Cervidae notebook would get the 133-byte LFS pointer, and\nzipfile raises BadZipFile. Install conda-forge''s git-lfs in the RTD\nenvironment and pull the LFS files first (checked on a clone made with\nGIT_LFS_SKIP_SMUDGE=1: the pointer becomes the 41 MB archive).\n\n* Use American spelling in the Cervidae robot test comments\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Santiago [C] Balestrini Robinson <sanbales@amazon.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx1tECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXncQAA0E+u3nRVehGsfpCo8k1jr1\nmJDusiRMqq51SvcA8ofv/A4giwXHWgR2TwXECaPq1LqfoUxvEyhxXfLqbdkyQoX9\nHmfVkl2ll1CoKqd58zcjpJYPE3wKiXLeu1EUi9s52BUMTJIzBAdPOM/IRgcrCurJ\nVzcufRy4jYy3oUS+gJD4Tgu0PUekXiYb1q1bSEJ3pF51QCJQhSjstqoKP7ivnZG1\n5Q7eto7u43yeo07un3I72bDRJCk+VN9um9KqC06pqNCGgWOzJekmiDfmUNbrNeaj\nWIm57Ge/SZq+t4ofFKlz5FDJ1T1mk9KfxJW6XJw9JLowpuZLNCjnI/r3gh/VcZDc\n9z0HxYDZ1l4ex/E7khBGKWorIJgxp9386S+OeHlQpLflGV7Bi8ATi1q3j7HDfK3n\nxubUlW7GWcqIGHJ+3HFYfQMaoLnX2mgWotwSh9Vv9dlP6bLxwiV9ICv067l2j2e+\nRalKAEStN0IM4y7lIbpKeODqwL7UNf/VnYvRRZ2u0hzqY1vF6hV37bshzefjg+TF\ntF5hktxZDmxaXkZRlC5O8wBiVWPoYxUGxlqG5ZDh/3+uzwd0k4E6ncbeDfV6TjAW\n2e/jmcZB6WJ6/GlVTuArKzZNUIRgpqKk8jci3mAZYwgs8cO3H1VjFaHiAeUKM6AJ\nH61WE09h7aiFicm57rMR\n=Wi5g\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T08:58:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commit/4c923de60343ed09aa537ad6fe955f4ea46b85fd","node_id":"C_kwDOEQFCU9oAKDRjOTIzZGU2MDM0M2VkMDlhYTUzN2FkNmZlOTU1ZjRlYTQ2Yjg1ZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commit/d2f06fe205d8737ced3f00b59ab545cd65044a1d","sha":"d2f06fe205d8737ced3f00b59ab545cd65044a1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commits/d2f06fe205d8737ced3f00b59ab545cd65044a1d"}],"sha":"4c923de60343ed09aa537ad6fe955f4ea46b85fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commits/4c923de60343ed09aa537ad6fe955f4ea46b85fd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6493354?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dfreeman06","id":6493354,"login":"dfreeman06","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0OTMzNTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commits/d2f06fe205d8737ced3f00b59ab545cd65044a1d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T17:42:47Z","email":"freeman.dane@gmail.com","name":"dfreeman06"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T17:42:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Close and detach the old pipeline when diagram.pipe is replaced (#188)\n\n* Track pipe replacement in the benchmark gate (#180)\n\nAdd a `replace` phase to scripts/bench_pipeline.py: after the other phases,\n3 rounds of `diagram.pipe = DefaultFlow()` plus a refresh, recording\n`live_widgets_added` (live widgets in the ipywidgets registry after\ngc.collect(), so opens minus closes). bench_check.py gates it, also for the\nslow-browser run since it does not depend on timing.\n\nThe baseline records today''s value: 111 live widgets per case (37 per\nreplacement), the leak #180 describes.\n\nThe phase un-hides the collapse phase''s nodes first: a fresh pipeline\nre-sizes every label, and the text sizer stub cannot deserialise a reply\nwhose edges point at hidden nodes.\n\n`fast nested:100 first bytes_b2k` moves 214297 -> 214409: real elkjs output\ncarries GWT''s `$H` object hash, a counter in the shared node process, and the\nflat case''s 3 extra layouts advance it before the nested case runs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Close and detach the old pipeline when diagram.pipe is replaced (#180)\n\n`Diagram._change_pipe` only cancelled the old pipe. Its sub-pipes, the\nintermediate MarkElementWidget/MarkIndex pairs, the text sizer''s CSS widget,\ntheir layouts and any status views stayed open, and the `style` dlink, the\nprogress bar and the tools'' `tee` kept the old pipeline reachable: 37 live\nwidgets per replacement, 99 with the status view shown.\n\nOwnership: a diagram owns the pipe assigned to it, whoever built it.\nReplacing `diagram.pipe` unlinks and unwires the old pipe, rewires the\ndiagram to the new one, then closes the old one. A pipe can only feed one\ndiagram anyway (its inlet is set to that diagram''s source), and closing only\ndiagram-built pipes would leak every `diagram.pipe = DefaultFlow()`.\n\n`Pipe.close()` closes what the pipe created -- default inlet/outlet marks and\ntheir indices, its status view -- and never a widget it was given, so the\ndiagram''s source (the old pipeline''s inlet) stays open. `Pipeline.close()`\nalso closes its sub-pipes; status views and StyledWidget close their parts.\n\n`style`, the progress bar and the tools now follow any assigned pipe, not just\nthe default one. The bench `replace` count drops from 111 to 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Refuse a closed pipe and pin in-flight replacement (#180 review)\n\n- `Diagram` validates `pipe`: assigning a closed pipe (swapping back to a\n  replaced one) raises `TraitError` before anything is rewired, instead of\n  failing half-way through the swap.\n- Test replacing the pipe mid-run: the old run is cancelled, its taken flow\n  is handed back to the source, and the old pipe sends nothing more.\n- Test that the progress bar follows the new pipe without a refresh, and that\n  a replaced pipe is collected with no event loop.\n- The style link reaches text sizers in nested pipelines.\n- Docstrings and changelog: a pipe belongs to one diagram; its sub-pipes are\n  closed with it; only an inlet/outlet passed in is left open.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Reword ''sizers'' for the Vale spelling gate\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Test the nested style link; shorten the mid-run resend wait\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Refuse a pipe another open diagram owns (#180 review)\n\nA pipe keeps a weak reference to the diagram that owns it. Assigning it to\nanother diagram, through `Diagram(pipe=...)` or `diagram.pipe = ...`, raises\n`TraitError` from the `pipe` validator before anything is wired, while the\nowner is open. Replacing the pipe or closing the owner releases it (a closed\ndiagram''s links, progress callback and claim are dropped); a collected owner\nreleases it through the weak reference. Only the top-level pipe is owned.\n\n`Diagram.close()` releases only a pipe it owns: a diagram whose constructor\nwas refused is closed when collected and must not touch the other diagram''s\npipe.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Refuse an owned pipe nested in the assigned pipe (#180 review)\n\nThe `pipe` validator now walks the assigned pipe breadth first, like\n`_wire_pipe`, and refuses it if any pipe in it is closed or owned by another\nopen diagram, so `Pipeline(pipes=[other.pipe])` cannot share a pipe either.\nA sub-pipe belongs to its pipeline.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Refuse wrapping the current pipe in its replacement (#180 review)\n\n`d.pipe = Pipeline(pipes=[d.pipe])` passed the ownership walk (the owner is\nthe diagram itself) and then closed the old pipe while the new one ran it.\nThe validator now refuses the current pipe nested in a new one. Also scope\nthe nested-refusal test to the refusal step and rewrap the docstring.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Own the whole pipe tree; refuse any reused part of it (#180 review)\n\nThe diagram now marks every pipe in the assigned tree as its own and clears\nevery mark when it releases the pipe. The `pipe` validator walks the new\ntree and refuses any pipe that is closed, owned by another open diagram, or\npart of the current pipe (which replacing it would close). This covers\nwrapping the current pipe, reusing its stages, and borrowing another\ndiagram''s sub-pipe; re-assigning the current pipe is still a no-op.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Refuse a stage added to the current pipe in place (#180 review)\n\nA stage added to the current pipeline after assignment carries no mark, so\nthe validator also refuses any pipe found in the current pipe''s tree by\nidentity. Document that changing an assigned pipeline''s `pipes` is not\ntracked.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dane <dane@Mac-Box.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9db3a28a10cbd66f38578fc473e34d68898edcfc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/git/trees/9db3a28a10cbd66f38578fc473e34d68898edcfc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/git/commits/d2f06fe205d8737ced3f00b59ab545cd65044a1d","verification":{"payload":"tree 9db3a28a10cbd66f38578fc473e34d68898edcfc\nparent 5eb6559b6d9751684f5a142ae21ee16a8d8c6b2c\nauthor dfreeman06 <freeman.dane@gmail.com> 1791135767 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791135767 -0400\n\nClose and detach the old pipeline when diagram.pipe is replaced (#188)\n\n* Track pipe replacement in the benchmark gate (#180)\n\nAdd a `replace` phase to scripts/bench_pipeline.py: after the other phases,\n3 rounds of `diagram.pipe = DefaultFlow()` plus a refresh, recording\n`live_widgets_added` (live widgets in the ipywidgets registry after\ngc.collect(), so opens minus closes). bench_check.py gates it, also for the\nslow-browser run since it does not depend on timing.\n\nThe baseline records today''s value: 111 live widgets per case (37 per\nreplacement), the leak #180 describes.\n\nThe phase un-hides the collapse phase''s nodes first: a fresh pipeline\nre-sizes every label, and the text sizer stub cannot deserialise a reply\nwhose edges point at hidden nodes.\n\n`fast nested:100 first bytes_b2k` moves 214297 -> 214409: real elkjs output\ncarries GWT''s `$H` object hash, a counter in the shared node process, and the\nflat case''s 3 extra layouts advance it before the nested case runs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Close and detach the old pipeline when diagram.pipe is replaced (#180)\n\n`Diagram._change_pipe` only cancelled the old pipe. Its sub-pipes, the\nintermediate MarkElementWidget/MarkIndex pairs, the text sizer''s CSS widget,\ntheir layouts and any status views stayed open, and the `style` dlink, the\nprogress bar and the tools'' `tee` kept the old pipeline reachable: 37 live\nwidgets per replacement, 99 with the status view shown.\n\nOwnership: a diagram owns the pipe assigned to it, whoever built it.\nReplacing `diagram.pipe` unlinks and unwires the old pipe, rewires the\ndiagram to the new one, then closes the old one. A pipe can only feed one\ndiagram anyway (its inlet is set to that diagram''s source), and closing only\ndiagram-built pipes would leak every `diagram.pipe = DefaultFlow()`.\n\n`Pipe.close()` closes what the pipe created -- default inlet/outlet marks and\ntheir indices, its status view -- and never a widget it was given, so the\ndiagram''s source (the old pipeline''s inlet) stays open. `Pipeline.close()`\nalso closes its sub-pipes; status views and StyledWidget close their parts.\n\n`style`, the progress bar and the tools now follow any assigned pipe, not just\nthe default one. The bench `replace` count drops from 111 to 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Refuse a closed pipe and pin in-flight replacement (#180 review)\n\n- `Diagram` validates `pipe`: assigning a closed pipe (swapping back to a\n  replaced one) raises `TraitError` before anything is rewired, instead of\n  failing half-way through the swap.\n- Test replacing the pipe mid-run: the old run is cancelled, its taken flow\n  is handed back to the source, and the old pipe sends nothing more.\n- Test that the progress bar follows the new pipe without a refresh, and that\n  a replaced pipe is collected with no event loop.\n- The style link reaches text sizers in nested pipelines.\n- Docstrings and changelog: a pipe belongs to one diagram; its sub-pipes are\n  closed with it; only an inlet/outlet passed in is left open.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Reword ''sizers'' for the Vale spelling gate\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Test the nested style link; shorten the mid-run resend wait\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Refuse a pipe another open diagram owns (#180 review)\n\nA pipe keeps a weak reference to the diagram that owns it. Assigning it to\nanother diagram, through `Diagram(pipe=...)` or `diagram.pipe = ...`, raises\n`TraitError` from the `pipe` validator before anything is wired, while the\nowner is open. Replacing the pipe or closing the owner releases it (a closed\ndiagram''s links, progress callback and claim are dropped); a collected owner\nreleases it through the weak reference. Only the top-level pipe is owned.\n\n`Diagram.close()` releases only a pipe it owns: a diagram whose constructor\nwas refused is closed when collected and must not touch the other diagram''s\npipe.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Refuse an owned pipe nested in the assigned pipe (#180 review)\n\nThe `pipe` validator now walks the assigned pipe breadth first, like\n`_wire_pipe`, and refuses it if any pipe in it is closed or owned by another\nopen diagram, so `Pipeline(pipes=[other.pipe])` cannot share a pipe either.\nA sub-pipe belongs to its pipeline.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Refuse wrapping the current pipe in its replacement (#180 review)\n\n`d.pipe = Pipeline(pipes=[d.pipe])` passed the ownership walk (the owner is\nthe diagram itself) and then closed the old pipe while the new one ran it.\nThe validator now refuses the current pipe nested in a new one. Also scope\nthe nested-refusal test to the refusal step and rewrap the docstring.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Own the whole pipe tree; refuse any reused part of it (#180 review)\n\nThe diagram now marks every pipe in the assigned tree as its own and clears\nevery mark when it releases the pipe. The `pipe` validator walks the new\ntree and refuses any pipe that is closed, owned by another open diagram, or\npart of the current pipe (which replacing it would close). This covers\nwrapping the current pipe, reusing its stages, and borrowing another\ndiagram''s sub-pipe; re-assigning the current pipe is still a no-op.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Refuse a stage added to the current pipe in place (#180 review)\n\nA stage added to the current pipeline after assignment carries no mark, so\nthe validator also refuses any pipe found in the current pipe''s tree by\nidentity. Document that changing an assigned pipeline''s `pipes` is not\ntracked.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dane <dane@Mac-Box.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwpAXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlE0QABZtGBYE23+l9/HBE+PMIRkn\nw5gSFo/ZgwryOGn2pko+5sR9c8BIZFBvY7Nqxt1cZszGkMhjWNLOS7J16GaQAb+5\nyLwxti7B5cJ1cyUQvle6xYYgofHK95Cgm31vkaqTF1XjAGyt219gms7RbfcALE6l\n/NUc2G0+0RyXuZln/UevNxzdwksrvhXdUZRLyi7IZdAo02v4VAW+UkrtUCnWxvnZ\nsx9krE+oonmWTAF233WZvQrckR6OpB+hQGtwlUgS6JgvYCrg3mN3UbevQs0JxgBO\nP6lWrWxYFNX6NQLXdXMIUSwsqOZB45AV5e1Bz+pZ6hY7CroVHkR8RSVHHSNb3Jo8\n19InlUEpeCawYs2qkXhf/syt47E6hdn4KiXKad5pMUvgz47Q9GLXOOP1ppuIPtH1\nELiH0EmYIzPOvSojwtNIDuPaqm/NNyxTBPO39xWqBy7RxugY7RGLy4Ycmr9kuifk\nFEEjnFefjN3N6NSKuiF9xD3KaRFv+rJTE36MquBU6I/x0hns/AYR97qFUTDDG0Ba\nMhxuyKb4ctMokL7TguD2fmS2COG0MikmgKKvg82JUrqWmo5bX1LK9JnnKm2VjKjc\nMpyoV+V26mN0DvjIs6w/Fz7pqrKz2r1URnEdpM5k+iOKf+Z2+/vdZvL/sBgVgrUM\nAx89UqQU1V+OJB78qkiI\n=kBRU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T17:42:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commit/d2f06fe205d8737ced3f00b59ab545cd65044a1d","node_id":"C_kwDOEQFCU9oAKGQyZjA2ZmUyMDVkODczN2NlZDNmMDBiNTlhYjU0NWNkNjUwNDRhMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commit/5eb6559b6d9751684f5a142ae21ee16a8d8c6b2c","sha":"5eb6559b6d9751684f5a142ae21ee16a8d8c6b2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commits/5eb6559b6d9751684f5a142ae21ee16a8d8c6b2c"}],"sha":"d2f06fe205d8737ced3f00b59ab545cd65044a1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commits/d2f06fe205d8737ced3f00b59ab545cd65044a1d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6493354?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dfreeman06","id":6493354,"login":"dfreeman06","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0OTMzNTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commits/5eb6559b6d9751684f5a142ae21ee16a8d8c6b2c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T16:32:08Z","email":"freeman.dane@gmail.com","name":"dfreeman06"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T16:32:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fade elements out once so a diagram can''t freeze on an update (#190)\n\n* Fade elements out once, so a diagram cannot freeze on an update (gh-95)\n\nSprotty''s FadeAnimation removes faded-out elements when the eased time\nreaches 1, but Animation only stops at raw time 1, and easeInOut rounds to\n1 within ~1e-8 of the end. A frame landing just short of the duration\nremoved the elements, the real last frame removed them again and threw\n\"No such child\" inside the animation-frame callback, the animation never\nsettled, and sprotty''s command stack waited on it forever: every later\nlayout arrived and was never drawn.\n\nUpdateModelCommand2 now builds a FadeOnceAnimation that only removes what\nis still attached.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Delegate the fade-once tween to sprotty and pin it mid-animation\n\nFadeOnceAnimation no longer copies sprotty''s tween loop: it skips any\ntween(1) after the first and hands everything else to FadeAnimation. The\ncommand builds that fade itself, so sprotty never builds one to replace.\nThe test now checks a mid-animation frame (both fades near 0.5, the\nfaded-out node still attached) and flags itself for deletion once\neclipse-sprotty/sprotty#573 is fixed, which the changelog now cites.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Check that an update without fades builds no fade animation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dane <dane@Mac-Box.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"65e2b0d5d378c012abc820f8c91128d1f76dd2b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/git/trees/65e2b0d5d378c012abc820f8c91128d1f76dd2b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/git/commits/5eb6559b6d9751684f5a142ae21ee16a8d8c6b2c","verification":{"payload":"tree 65e2b0d5d378c012abc820f8c91128d1f76dd2b5\nparent 2a7b56fb7526ffd152a02f8383378494c2a674c7\nauthor dfreeman06 <freeman.dane@gmail.com> 1791131528 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791131528 -0400\n\nFade elements out once so a diagram can''t freeze on an update (#190)\n\n* Fade elements out once, so a diagram cannot freeze on an update (gh-95)\n\nSprotty''s FadeAnimation removes faded-out elements when the eased time\nreaches 1, but Animation only stops at raw time 1, and easeInOut rounds to\n1 within ~1e-8 of the end. A frame landing just short of the duration\nremoved the elements, the real last frame removed them again and threw\n\"No such child\" inside the animation-frame callback, the animation never\nsettled, and sprotty''s command stack waited on it forever: every later\nlayout arrived and was never drawn.\n\nUpdateModelCommand2 now builds a FadeOnceAnimation that only removes what\nis still attached.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Delegate the fade-once tween to sprotty and pin it mid-animation\n\nFadeOnceAnimation no longer copies sprotty''s tween loop: it skips any\ntween(1) after the first and hands everything else to FadeAnimation. The\ncommand builds that fade itself, so sprotty never builds one to replace.\nThe test now checks a mid-animation frame (both fades near 0.5, the\nfaded-out node still attached) and flags itself for deletion once\neclipse-sprotty/sprotty#573 is fixed, which the changelog now cites.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Check that an update without fades builds no fade animation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dane <dane@Mac-Box.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwn+ICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAORoQAD6GN41OvB7e4K+eZ6d9qHDM\nK1dPPp1MPAKvhJ+reqcluiwk2e2edob8wIoQx2vnYszVnWqtoK8dfnWcOL+WUWgI\nrxiUZCSlA9sCVlrPvM5u00+P6n8OAPaQhYjRorz6FtyGOTtxYOEqEIUyMjXLxCbH\nktoXhWS18ySoPJfJ2T7RC9fXCNVxf9uBkydA4/DowF3A2vtbUnF7j3mIGXKATdC8\ngfFICOjsyHBO+BQu/JyV9QpRpje2NWrklo1HdeFJkfOWJI/h62W7kWQ0zdIoKfbX\n7u/O8V0NTX8hfK1pKiOCQpWrSxJbOYgDs+i5JeO8T+kr5+cQY57lZe9yfmHPD1XE\nPnW2a9Rdi7XDk8JOT0iP3+omyeAAv0E82po9yd/v6kbWQyksaJb62hovQRqIyIyH\n+NMy38BCW/0PBgktf5SADV74vymxhd/PN/ajZ08aanGIE9Y5siaixQmMxUfG4S4l\nvKyxmhKAB1aJQw92xfWtTiSP6oRbAudYnlgQTYlzZMZEcgEaxNyhOlhbBD+04tQI\nICXz8PpkLQtiivXKGRxQm9gLPUMA/YpkOcfRLe6egKdh7SQDFfm2P890a6Ty+JbT\nh433pX01pxrlMvudfH6FAq5LUHWxAFbKQBFr6CEYDH81OIVYW2aMRiYLtQ3sh4c8\nUnQ/tk9mxDrk9VieivYx\n=fBV5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T16:32:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commit/5eb6559b6d9751684f5a142ae21ee16a8d8c6b2c","node_id":"C_kwDOEQFCU9oAKDVlYjY1NTliNmQ5NzUxNjg0ZjVhMTQyYWUyMWVlMTZhOGQ4YzZiMmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commit/2a7b56fb7526ffd152a02f8383378494c2a674c7","sha":"2a7b56fb7526ffd152a02f8383378494c2a674c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commits/2a7b56fb7526ffd152a02f8383378494c2a674c7"}],"sha":"5eb6559b6d9751684f5a142ae21ee16a8d8c6b2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commits/5eb6559b6d9751684f5a142ae21ee16a8d8c6b2c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6493354?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dfreeman06","id":6493354,"login":"dfreeman06","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0OTMzNTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commits/2a7b56fb7526ffd152a02f8383378494c2a674c7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T12:52:34Z","email":"freeman.dane@gmail.com","name":"dfreeman06"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T12:52:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add a robot regression test for the #95 slider-burst race (#186)\n\n* Add a robot test that bursts the 04_Interactive sliders (gh-95)\n\nSteps number_of_nodes and seed one key at a time, five bursts in a row,\nthen waits for the kernel''s elk.source to hold the last requested graph\nand for the DOM to draw it, without touching the collapse toggle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Fingerprint the graph in the slider-burst test, fold it into 04_Interactive\n\n- The kernel check compared node, edge, label and port counts, which only\n  depend on number_of_nodes, so an elk.source one seed step behind passed.\n  A probe module now fingerprints elk.source''s edges by the nodes they join\n  and compares that with the graph make_graph builds for the kernel''s\n  slider values; the page check compares the drawn edges'' DOM ids with\n  elk.source''s edge ids, uuids that are fresh on every load.\n- Bursts end on number_of_nodes, seed or percent_of_edges.\n- The probe is imported once; each check types a short `_k95(\"<token>\")`,\n  and the log shows when elk.source last changed and when the drawing\n  matched, relative to the end of the burst.\n- The bursts run in the existing 04_Interactive test: one restart.\n- `Run IPyElk Code In A New Cell` activated the notebook with a click on\n  its centre, which selected a diagram node (see #182); it now clicks the\n  last cell''s prompt, so new cells also land in order. Its screenshot name\n  is an argument.\n\nRefs #95\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Warn about acceptance tests that only passed on a retry\n\nATEST_RETRIES re-runs failed tests, so an intermittent failure turns the\njob green without a trace outside the artifacts. After a passing run,\nname each test that failed on an earlier attempt as a GitHub warning.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Give the slider bursts 60 s to converge\n\nOn macos-latest the kernel ran up to ~40 s behind a burst, and the ElkJS\npipe''s 30 s wait for a layout from the browser timed out once per failing\nattempt; the 30 s budget failed 04_Interactive on 2 of 3 attempts there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Skip the gh-95 bursts on failure on macos-latest, and warn about it\n\nOn macos-latest the kernel stopped answering for over 60 s after a burst,\nwith the ElkJS pipe in \"30s error\", on 3 of 5 attempts over two runs; the\nother five jobs passed first time. Report that as a skip there instead of\ngating on it, and raise skips as GitHub warnings along with tests that\nonly passed on a retry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Skip the gh-95 bursts on failure on macos-14 too; keep the view in sight\n\ntest-oldest (macos-14) failed a first attempt with the page still drawing\nan older 81-edge graph for a minute while elk.source held the 100-edge\none. Both macOS runners now report the bursts as a skip and a warning;\nLinux and Windows passed every first attempt and still gate.\n\nScroll the view into sight on every drawing check: Sprotty only draws\nedges in view, and the notebook may scroll to a new cell meanwhile.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Gate the gh-95 bursts only on the current Linux and Windows jobs\n\nAfter the rebase, test-oldest (ubuntu-latest) failed 2 of 3 attempts\nbefore any burst: the probe''s import cell never ran, with the kernel\nreading \"Idle\" and the pipe in \"30s error\". Over four CI runs the\nbursts passed every first attempt on test (ubuntu-latest) and\ntest (windows-latest), and test-oldest (windows-latest); they hung on a\nfirst attempt on macos-latest (2 runs), macos-14 (1) and test-oldest\n(ubuntu-latest) (1). Skip on failure, with a warning, on macOS and in\nevery oldest job.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Skip only the gh-95 bursts, and say why each job skips them\n\n- Tag the test `gh:95` only once the notebook has run, so the notebook''s\n  own checks still fail, not skip, on the skip-on-failure jobs.\n- Skip on failure only on macOS (#95, until the sprotty FadeAnimation fix\n  lands) and test-oldest (ubuntu-latest) (#177, until the kernel stall is\n  understood); test-oldest (windows-latest) passed every first attempt.\n- When the probe gets no answer, report the check cell''s prompt and the\n  pipe status, so a stalled kernel and a wedged page tell apart in the\n  warning; drop Robot''s retry preamble from the message.\n- End burst 2 on number_of_nodes: at 5 nodes, neighboring seeds can\n  build the same graph.\n- Run check cells in place, so no empty cell is left after each one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Name both hangs behind the macOS skip of the gh-95 bursts\n\nThe macOS failures are page wedges (#95) and kernel stalls (#177); the\nskip stays until both are fixed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dane <dane@Mac-Box.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ce7ac31201663fe9f8a90615ecf05a6f0b77f833","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/git/trees/ce7ac31201663fe9f8a90615ecf05a6f0b77f833"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/git/commits/2a7b56fb7526ffd152a02f8383378494c2a674c7","verification":{"payload":"tree ce7ac31201663fe9f8a90615ecf05a6f0b77f833\nparent 2c1fb23f27e91fc842d7fafc478039ea0a902f26\nauthor dfreeman06 <freeman.dane@gmail.com> 1791118354 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791118354 -0400\n\nAdd a robot regression test for the #95 slider-burst race (#186)\n\n* Add a robot test that bursts the 04_Interactive sliders (gh-95)\n\nSteps number_of_nodes and seed one key at a time, five bursts in a row,\nthen waits for the kernel''s elk.source to hold the last requested graph\nand for the DOM to draw it, without touching the collapse toggle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Fingerprint the graph in the slider-burst test, fold it into 04_Interactive\n\n- The kernel check compared node, edge, label and port counts, which only\n  depend on number_of_nodes, so an elk.source one seed step behind passed.\n  A probe module now fingerprints elk.source''s edges by the nodes they join\n  and compares that with the graph make_graph builds for the kernel''s\n  slider values; the page check compares the drawn edges'' DOM ids with\n  elk.source''s edge ids, uuids that are fresh on every load.\n- Bursts end on number_of_nodes, seed or percent_of_edges.\n- The probe is imported once; each check types a short `_k95(\"<token>\")`,\n  and the log shows when elk.source last changed and when the drawing\n  matched, relative to the end of the burst.\n- The bursts run in the existing 04_Interactive test: one restart.\n- `Run IPyElk Code In A New Cell` activated the notebook with a click on\n  its centre, which selected a diagram node (see #182); it now clicks the\n  last cell''s prompt, so new cells also land in order. Its screenshot name\n  is an argument.\n\nRefs #95\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Warn about acceptance tests that only passed on a retry\n\nATEST_RETRIES re-runs failed tests, so an intermittent failure turns the\njob green without a trace outside the artifacts. After a passing run,\nname each test that failed on an earlier attempt as a GitHub warning.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Give the slider bursts 60 s to converge\n\nOn macos-latest the kernel ran up to ~40 s behind a burst, and the ElkJS\npipe''s 30 s wait for a layout from the browser timed out once per failing\nattempt; the 30 s budget failed 04_Interactive on 2 of 3 attempts there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2