://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dfreeman06","id":6493354,"login":"dfreeman06","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0OTMzNTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commits/2c1fb23f27e91fc842d7fafc478039ea0a902f26/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T01:18:36Z","email":"freeman.dane@gmail.com","name":"dfreeman06"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T01:18:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Make Vale a real prose linter: lint sources, add style rules, gate CI (#185)\n\n* Fix typos and non-US spellings in source prose\n\nTypos, British spellings and term casing found by the Vale source lint\n(#181) in docstrings, comments, notebook markdown and the changelog.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Lint source prose with Vale in the lint job\n\n`lint-vale` lints root *.md, docs, src docstrings and comments, and\nnotebook markdown (extracted by `nblint.py --extract-only`) without a\nSphinx build, adds the proselint and write-good styles from conda-forge,\nkeeps only the en_US dictionary, and fails on any warning or error.\n`check-spelling`, which linted built HTML and always exited 0, is\nremoved.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Document the Vale prose lint\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Fix term casing and typos in src, tests and scripts prose\n\nCSS/HTML/JSON/DOM/JupyterLab casing in docstrings and comments, and\ntypos in tests and scripts, found once Vale.Terms runs on Python and\ntests/ and scripts/ are linted (#181 review).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Keep Vale.Terms on for Python and fix vocabulary casing\n\nLowercase vocabulary entries become [Xx]ord or (?i) so they may start a\nsentence; RST literals that trip Vale.Terms get exact vocabulary\nentries instead of the rule being off for every .py file. Drop the\nredundant E-Prime switch and write-good.Illusions (duplicates\nVale.Repetition), keep released changelog notes as written, widen task\ninputs, and document a working inline disable plus the Python route.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Fail vale_lint when Vale crashes or lints nothing\n\nA non-zero Vale exit, empty output or output that isn''t\n{path: [alert, ...]} now exits 2 with Vale''s stderr, as does a missing\nor empty lint path. Lint tests/ and scripts/ too, check a .py canary\nas well as .md, and test the exit codes with a fake vale.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Document PipeStatusView.html as a widget and note the ui vocab trade-off\n\nAlso accept the terms that module-docstring linting surfaces (IPython,\nnbconvert, pytest, stderr, utest, JSON file paths and attributes).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Lint module docstrings that follow the license header\n\nVale skips a module docstring after a `#` comment, which hid 37 of 52.\nvale_lint copies each module docstring, on its original lines, to\nbuild/vale_docstrings and reports findings against the source file. A\nheader-led .py canary guards it; the fake-vale tests now also kill the\ncanary, return-code, empty-output, key-shape and mapping mutants.\nFixes the GB spellings this surfaced.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Re-lock pixi.lock on master after #184\n\nTaken from master and re-solved with pixi; the only changes are the\nvale packages (vale 3.24.0, en_US dictionary, proselint and write-good\nstyles) and vale''s win-64 runtime builds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Move the ui vocabulary note to vale.ini; recommend [**/file.py]\n\naccept.txt has no comments (a # line is a regex), and a [**/file.py]\nsection also covers the module docstring''s copy under\nbuild/vale_docstrings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Exit 2 naming the file when a module can''t be parsed\n\nA SyntaxError or non-UTF-8 .py file raised out of vale_lint with exit\n1, which reads as findings. Also pin stale-copy removal, numeric\nsorting and the str-docstring check with tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dane <dane@Mac-Box.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b2efabb6239bb47d5594601470d5345253c72ef6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/git/trees/b2efabb6239bb47d5594601470d5345253c72ef6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/git/commits/2c1fb23f27e91fc842d7fafc478039ea0a902f26","verification":{"payload":"tree b2efabb6239bb47d5594601470d5345253c72ef6\nparent 20c7cb600f721d78ed041dd960f2d57eb0183590\nauthor dfreeman06 <freeman.dane@gmail.com> 1791076716 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791076716 -0400\n\nMake Vale a real prose linter: lint sources, add style rules, gate CI (#185)\n\n* Fix typos and non-US spellings in source prose\n\nTypos, British spellings and term casing found by the Vale source lint\n(#181) in docstrings, comments, notebook markdown and the changelog.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Lint source prose with Vale in the lint job\n\n`lint-vale` lints root *.md, docs, src docstrings and comments, and\nnotebook markdown (extracted by `nblint.py --extract-only`) without a\nSphinx build, adds the proselint and write-good styles from conda-forge,\nkeeps only the en_US dictionary, and fails on any warning or error.\n`check-spelling`, which linted built HTML and always exited 0, is\nremoved.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Document the Vale prose lint\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Fix term casing and typos in src, tests and scripts prose\n\nCSS/HTML/JSON/DOM/JupyterLab casing in docstrings and comments, and\ntypos in tests and scripts, found once Vale.Terms runs on Python and\ntests/ and scripts/ are linted (#181 review).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Keep Vale.Terms on for Python and fix vocabulary casing\n\nLowercase vocabulary entries become [Xx]ord or (?i) so they may start a\nsentence; RST literals that trip Vale.Terms get exact vocabulary\nentries instead of the rule being off for every .py file. Drop the\nredundant E-Prime switch and write-good.Illusions (duplicates\nVale.Repetition), keep released changelog notes as written, widen task\ninputs, and document a working inline disable plus the Python route.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Fail vale_lint when Vale crashes or lints nothing\n\nA non-zero Vale exit, empty output or output that isn''t\n{path: [alert, ...]} now exits 2 with Vale''s stderr, as does a missing\nor empty lint path. Lint tests/ and scripts/ too, check a .py canary\nas well as .md, and test the exit codes with a fake vale.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Document PipeStatusView.html as a widget and note the ui vocab trade-off\n\nAlso accept the terms that module-docstring linting surfaces (IPython,\nnbconvert, pytest, stderr, utest, JSON file paths and attributes).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Lint module docstrings that follow the license header\n\nVale skips a module docstring after a `#` comment, which hid 37 of 52.\nvale_lint copies each module docstring, on its original lines, to\nbuild/vale_docstrings and reports findings against the source file. A\nheader-led .py canary guards it; the fake-vale tests now also kill the\ncanary, return-code, empty-output, key-shape and mapping mutants.\nFixes the GB spellings this surfaced.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Re-lock pixi.lock on master after #184\n\nTaken from master and re-solved with pixi; the only changes are the\nvale packages (vale 3.24.0, en_US dictionary, proselint and write-good\nstyles) and vale''s win-64 runtime builds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Move the ui vocabulary note to vale.ini; recommend [**/file.py]\n\naccept.txt has no comments (a # line is a regex), and a [**/file.py]\nsection also covers the module docstring''s copy under\nbuild/vale_docstrings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Exit 2 naming the file when a module can''t be parsed\n\nA SyntaxError or non-UTF-8 .py file raised out of vale_lint with exit\n1, which reads as findings. Also pin stale-copy removal, numeric\nsorting and the str-docstring check with tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dane <dane@Mac-Box.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwalsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiK8QAKAzlajacuvKRXebGRkCqYi5\nNulSTYhwcewFkLAJQKrDtHeyEvM/MUlFB7ftFuc+JwmNVG4W65pbOuoSuO55CGQE\nnZJPwsqeI+ywiEjxjJVnRJtyFEMEZU5PvEe6IqU+n1j3lpRlDK1wo+rQrbACwX48\nVJf2kRLkoAoIkY3kkNBZ3AIFPAInKesEcop8u+fd7j9fMSpzhZC9m54z0CM87rgj\nOP326UxwZPgHb9TPNh9L/2wHJJyTXVJelfDSEGPoW1w3O3rPT8n7w6+Cs+B8ux+O\nTyZ0FJ+o0gOkpiV7+Mt3dXcTKUGwQxLKZ/mEvDoO9fXXt67puoidgYikDf6fDgTQ\nyF7z1jxO48hwfJM6cTf8sKRrtHvXfj10CNy3dpCF0uvkQEpFUvr7NOBhHCMSnkBT\nDznKqDFcfUo/8M4s8RZR/L0WgeV5XqT8+CaxZH3dompzaPsR0mjUEhy9UH2ZvZdc\nF65GI/R/12M5ZPRz8bVYyQb03DkoWvOJ0r6rbLI2UGqg75bCrwLtoDOu46arlD39\n3BtUYErBBX6hO8NvGqkyMRNi8noghH8o6U1SkVs65RMP7HUVmNsLdLHMkMYfU28U\ncNrBmlHZ54jj2sPxzwwfKY6jhNkI33YfoGwRAcGWMmLN17Y3Grdwd7rI1ZT4/waC\nqr612SQkBgspo2l+R7nG\n=17se\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T01:18:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commit/2c1fb23f27e91fc842d7fafc478039ea0a902f26","node_id":"C_kwDOEQFCU9oAKDJjMWZiMjNmMjdlOTFmYzg0MmQ3ZmFmYzQ3ODAzOWVhMGE5MDJmMjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commit/20c7cb600f721d78ed041dd960f2d57eb0183590","sha":"20c7cb600f721d78ed041dd960f2d57eb0183590","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commits/20c7cb600f721d78ed041dd960f2d57eb0183590"}],"sha":"2c1fb23f27e91fc842d7fafc478039ea0a902f26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commits/2c1fb23f27e91fc842d7fafc478039ea0a902f26"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6493354?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dfreeman06","id":6493354,"login":"dfreeman06","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0OTMzNTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commits/20c7cb600f721d78ed041dd960f2d57eb0183590/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T00:00:46Z","email":"freeman.dane@gmail.com","name":"dfreeman06"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T00:00:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add ast-grep structural lint rules (#184)\n\n* Take the running loop in wait_for_answer\n\n`wait_for_answer` is only called from the `browser_roundtrip` coroutine, so\n`asyncio.get_running_loop()` returns the same loop `get_event_loop()` did,\nand fails loudly instead of binding to some other loop if that ever changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Add ast-grep structural lint rules\n\n`pixi run lint-ast-grep` (part of `pixi run lint`) first runs `ast-grep test`\nover each rule''s valid/invalid cases, then scans the Python and TypeScript\nsources. The nine rules cover hazards ruff, mypy and tsc do not check:\n`asyncio.get_event_loop()`, `suppress(Exception)`, synced `Instance` traits\nwithout a serializer, `observe()` without trait names, unguarded debug\nlogging, string evaluation, `debugger`, `@ts-ignore`, and markup sinks.\n\nThe intended markup sinks (svg/html/foreignObject shapes, the text sizer\nscaffold), the startup notice in patches.ts and the public `wait_for_change`\nhelper are suppressed with their reasons.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Document the ast-grep rules\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Take wait_for_change''s timer loop from its future\n\n`future.get_loop()` is the loop `asyncio.Future()` bound to, which is what\n`get_event_loop()` returned here, so the py-no-get-event-loop suppression\ngoes away. The helper has no callers left in the repo but stays importable\nfrom `ipyelk.pipes.util`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Guard the Reflect.metadata notice with ELK_DEBUG\n\nThe \"skipping patch\" info printed on every normal page load. The text\nsizer''s markup suppression now gives the real reason: the interpolated CSS\nis the user''s style, trusted like `StyledWidget._css_widget`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Close coverage gaps in the ast-grep rules\n\n- ts-console-needs-elk-debug: only `&&` chains, `if`/ternary consequences\n  and `if (!ELK_DEBUG) return;` count as guards; `window.`/`globalThis.`/\n  `self.` receivers, `?.`, `console[''log'']` and the remaining debug methods\n  (count, group, time, dirxml, ...) are covered\n- ts-no-eval: `window.eval`, `(0, eval)`, `Function()`, `new\n  window.Function`, string-built timer code on any global\n- ts-no-html-injection: subscript and `+=` writes, `setHTMLUnsafe`,\n  `parseHTMLUnsafe`, `createContextualFragment`, `document.writeln`, any\n  `*.document.write`; `innerHTML: undefined/null` is allowed\n- py-no-get-event-loop: bare and any-receiver calls except `self.`\n- py-no-broad-suppress: nested and qualified `Exception` arguments\n- py-observe-all-traits: `names=None` and `type=` only; splats allowed\n- py-synced-instance-needs-serializer: only `*_serialization` splats\n  count; `Instance(dict)` and other JSON builtins are allowed\n- new py/ts-suppression-needs-rule-id rules, and `--error=unused-suppression`\n- pin ast-grep to 0.45.x (lock unchanged at 0.45.3)\n\nRule tests now kill every non-equivalent mutant of the rules.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Document suppression enforcement and the notebook gap\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Reject bare trailing ast-grep suppressions outside the scan\n\nA bare `ast-grep-ignore` at the end of a line silences every rule on that\nline, including the one meant to flag it, so `ast-grep scan` cannot catch\nit. `scripts/check_suppressions.py` greps the tracked .py/.ts/.tsx files\nfor a suppression without a rule id and runs last in `lint-ast-grep`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Drop false positives from the ast-grep rule rewrites\n\n- ts-no-eval: a timer''s string must be the argument or a direct operand of\n  a string concatenation, not anywhere inside it\n- ts-no-html-injection: `''''`, `undefined` and `null` are inert, as an\n  assignment or a prop value\n- py-no-broad-suppress: only direct arguments, tuple/list/splat elements\n  and `builtins.Exception`, not calls or other attributes\n- py-observe-all-traits: a positional `None` means all traits, like\n  `names=None`\n- ts-console-needs-elk-debug: cases for the early-return guard shape,\n  `profile`/`profileEnd`/`timeStamp` and `window?.console`\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* List the accepted ast-grep rule gaps\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dane <dane@Mac-Box.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1eb464932dfe54d4965a3e49c0fe75275d7568a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/git/trees/1eb464932dfe54d4965a3e49c0fe75275d7568a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/git/commits/20c7cb600f721d78ed041dd960f2d57eb0183590","verification":{"payload":"tree 1eb464932dfe54d4965a3e49c0fe75275d7568a6\nparent 00f48e1f59dec2009fa3fc47e5fda5fdd15dba49\nauthor dfreeman06 <freeman.dane@gmail.com> 1791072046 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791072046 -0400\n\nAdd ast-grep structural lint rules (#184)\n\n* Take the running loop in wait_for_answer\n\n`wait_for_answer` is only called from the `browser_roundtrip` coroutine, so\n`asyncio.get_running_loop()` returns the same loop `get_event_loop()` did,\nand fails loudly instead of binding to some other loop if that ever changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Add ast-grep structural lint rules\n\n`pixi run lint-ast-grep` (part of `pixi run lint`) first runs `ast-grep test`\nover each rule''s valid/invalid cases, then scans the Python and TypeScript\nsources. The nine rules cover hazards ruff, mypy and tsc do not check:\n`asyncio.get_event_loop()`, `suppress(Exception)`, synced `Instance` traits\nwithout a serializer, `observe()` without trait names, unguarded debug\nlogging, string evaluation, `debugger`, `@ts-ignore`, and markup sinks.\n\nThe intended markup sinks (svg/html/foreignObject shapes, the text sizer\nscaffold), the startup notice in patches.ts and the public `wait_for_change`\nhelper are suppressed with their reasons.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Document the ast-grep rules\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Take wait_for_change''s timer loop from its future\n\n`future.get_loop()` is the loop `asyncio.Future()` bound to, which is what\n`get_event_loop()` returned here, so the py-no-get-event-loop suppression\ngoes away. The helper has no callers left in the repo but stays importable\nfrom `ipyelk.pipes.util`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Guard the Reflect.metadata notice with ELK_DEBUG\n\nThe \"skipping patch\" info printed on every normal page load. The text\nsizer''s markup suppression now gives the real reason: the interpolated CSS\nis the user''s style, trusted like `StyledWidget._css_widget`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Close coverage gaps in the ast-grep rules\n\n- ts-console-needs-elk-debug: only `&&` chains, `if`/ternary consequences\n  and `if (!ELK_DEBUG) return;` count as guards; `window.`/`globalThis.`/\n  `self.` receivers, `?.`, `console[''log'']` and the remaining debug methods\n  (count, group, time, dirxml, ...) are covered\n- ts-no-eval: `window.eval`, `(0, eval)`, `Function()`, `new\n  window.Function`, string-built timer code on any global\n- ts-no-html-injection: subscript and `+=` writes, `setHTMLUnsafe`,\n  `parseHTMLUnsafe`, `createContextualFragment`, `document.writeln`, any\n  `*.document.write`; `innerHTML: undefined/null` is allowed\n- py-no-get-event-loop: bare and any-receiver calls except `self.`\n- py-no-broad-suppress: nested and qualified `Exception` arguments\n- py-observe-all-traits: `names=None` and `type=` only; splats allowed\n- py-synced-instance-needs-serializer: only `*_serialization` splats\n  count; `Instance(dict)` and other JSON builtins are allowed\n- new py/ts-suppression-needs-rule-id rules, and `--error=unused-suppression`\n- pin ast-grep to 0.45.x (lock unchanged at 0.45.3)\n\nRule tests now kill every non-equivalent mutant of the rules.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Document suppression enforcement and the notebook gap\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Reject bare trailing ast-grep suppressions outside the scan\n\nA bare `ast-grep-ignore` at the end of a line silences every rule on that\nline, including the one meant to flag it, so `ast-grep scan` cannot catch\nit. `scripts/check_suppressions.py` greps the tracked .py/.ts/.tsx files\nfor a suppression without a rule id and runs last in `lint-ast-grep`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Drop false positives from the ast-grep rule rewrites\n\n- ts-no-eval: a timer''s string must be the argument or a direct operand of\n  a string concatenation, not anywhere inside it\n- ts-no-html-injection: `''''`, `undefined` and `null` are inert, as an\n  assignment or a prop value\n- py-no-broad-suppress: only direct arguments, tuple/list/splat elements\n  and `builtins.Exception`, not calls or other attributes\n- py-observe-all-traits: a positional `None` means all traits, like\n  `names=None`\n- ts-console-needs-elk-debug: cases for the early-return guard shape,\n  `profile`/`profileEnd`/`timeStamp` and `window?.console`\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* List the accepted ast-grep rule gaps\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dane <dane@Mac-Box.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwZcuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYUgQAIIlRDAp2IqcEm44uPPRFxBv\nslG2J3Wz1b656p9mTD5Ht2umdyvHC9y1LGjC79O+V7G7OkCI5c7SYvUFLbNsmlrI\ncB89EevoIgWbSuJ+pKcpmQ1yJkOZeZJV7NrXIyvZrKGTTUrcu8fbkMJP+qblRUkf\nYJ5vS0PAOgak+a6kZxglX9yd5CBGetM3vnYcIIz80f1i5Jdw45EFcWsIeNFKvBrW\nJ9isO64jSWLzRoD0X9wkVneohUD+vlV+qdf/u0ARmQ8mP3tZP6sxpB0IgF6YD7lj\n4cgzCFx7yqQ5V2+Oq+22v6Q2hlNCHUUhSyyuxM3HKA7qSXWfvRwD2l6MxX6aom6C\n3DBFoOAMq13/Hs/F0+yasgSElEJ6a99z0mNV+WmhA0Oi4Pk+i3Qm8x93ThCZAfKi\nyZThP89sv+zhruaMsxNBl1S29b4OhSwVdpyUTZGzFGbVT0GaRGXlbWM/4iOxhZIv\nj2ZnZSu+h50TsLpWzX3MZ+wX6Uhccq32MP3NeLkIzC/IVCvrqojnuGmaHneqCdOO\naSCHzjNM1hgFqWQdFCFJUY+l1HbfU8bilQyZC9zyvkHWmotNp3pdbkxzPrLqS68a\nZyR+oGEO3rvEB1RmP5kF8MLCMY25abmq+Ep13oXpjs+eIFVWfHoLMhpR29ePlu8l\nhJo+eX7Uhe7AIkYuj+aP\n=CvRH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T00:00:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commit/20c7cb600f721d78ed041dd960f2d57eb0183590","node_id":"C_kwDOEQFCU9oAKDIwYzdjYjYwMGY3MjFkNzhlZDA0MWRkOTYwZjJkNTdlYjAxODM1OTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commit/00f48e1f59dec2009fa3fc47e5fda5fdd15dba49","sha":"00f48e1f59dec2009fa3fc47e5fda5fdd15dba49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commits/00f48e1f59dec2009fa3fc47e5fda5fdd15dba49"}],"sha":"20c7cb600f721d78ed041dd960f2d57eb0183590","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commits/20c7cb600f721d78ed041dd960f2d57eb0183590"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1438114?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanbales/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanbales/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanbales/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanbales/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sanbales","id":1438114,"login":"sanbales","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzgxMTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanbales/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanbales/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanbales/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanbales/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanbales/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sanbales","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commits/00f48e1f59dec2009fa3fc47e5fda5fdd15dba49/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:59:08Z","email":"sanbales@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Santiago Balestrini-Robinson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:59:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: preserve hidden projection state and unique label ids (#182)\n\nFixes #171:\n\n- A hidden port''s properties survive its slack projection coming back from\n  layout: `ElementIndex.update` no longer copies `slack-port` styling onto the\n  hidden source port.\n- An explicitly identified label that wraps to several lines gives each line\n  its own derived id (`<id>.<n>`) instead of sharing the parent''s.\n- The ELK JSON schema allows the slack-port lookup key.\n\nHeadless runs now pass the graph through instead of failing. With\n`IPYELK_NO_BROWSER` set (`nbconvert --execute`) there is no frontend to lay the\ngraph out, so `ElkJS.run` hands its inlet value on unlaid-out and the refresh\nsucceeds, the way `BrowserTextSizer` already falls back to its estimator. That\nfallback now also applies under `IPYELK_NO_BROWSER`, not only `IPYELK_TESTING`.\nThe check lives in the pipes'' own `run` methods, where `browser_roundtrip`\nalready reads the variable live, so the benchmark''s stubbed pipes (which\nreplace `run`) are unaffected. Converting the 16 example notebooks headless:\n31 \"Diagram refresh failed\" warnings and 93 TimeoutError traceback lines\nbefore, none after; bench counts unchanged from the baseline.\n\nSelect a node on purpose, and nowhere by accident, in the acceptance tests.\nThe JS coverage gate failed on this PR by 1.5 points: the 47 missing lines\nwere the browser-side selection and control-overlay code (renderer.tsx\ngetSelected / renderJLOverlayControl, display_widget.ts''s selection\nwrite-back, select.ts). On master those lines ran only because three shared\nkeywords clicked the centre of a diagram -- `Click Elk Tool` on the app and\nthen on the notebook (which it had just scrolled the app to the centre of),\nand `Create Linked Elk Output View` on the view -- and so selected whatever\nnode the layout had put there. When the diagram sat at the origin instead (a\nfrontend race, also seen on #162) nothing was selected and the gate failed.\nThose clicks are gone: the toolbar shows on `:hover` and needed no click, and\nSprotty ignores the right button, so the context menu needed none either.\n03_App now selects n1 deliberately (`Select Elk Node`: a pointer click on the\nnode''s label, then Sprotty''s `selected` class) and waits for the kernel''s\ncontrol-overlay button, so the round trip is asserted rather than hoped for.\nChecked with the full suite locally: 16/16 pass and the selection code runs in\n03_App and in no other suite.\n\nThe deliberate selection runs only where coverage is measured. On the `oldest`\nfrontend (JupyterLab 4.1.8, ipywidgets 8.0.1) selecting a node runs Firefox\nout of memory within seconds, on all three platforms: CI artifacts show the\nbrowser dying right after the first click, and the same accidental selection\nis what took `test-oldest (ubuntu-latest)` to GitHub''s 6-hour limit twice on\nmaster in one day (02_Transformer, right after the view''s centre click). That\nis a real defect for users on old frontends and is filed separately; removing\nthe accidental clicks stops it from hanging CI.\n\nBound every notebook suite to ten minutes. When the browser dies, geckodriver\nstops answering and the teardown spends ~10 minutes per Selenium call on\nurllib3 retries; Robot''s `Test Timeout` does not cover teardown. pabot runs one\nnotebook suite per process; `--processtimeout 600` kills a suite (setup, test\nand teardown) that overruns, with no orphaned browser or driver left behind\n(checked locally with a 20-second timeout). `Test Timeout` drops to 8 minutes\nso a hung test still fails as a Robot failure, with its screenshot, before the\nprocess is killed; the longest wait inside a test is 5 minutes. The CI step\nkeeps a 45-minute wall clock as the outer belt. Two waits that a loaded macOS\nrunner (four browsers on three cores) kept missing are retried or longer: the\nfile browser is refreshed until it lists a just-copied notebook (five of nine\nfailures in one macOS run were this), and the control-overlay button gets 30 s.\n\nMake the headless kernel wedge diagnosable. `itest-oldest-nbconvert` fails\nabout one run in five, across branches, always the same way: `03_App.ipynb`,\nthe cell after `display(box)`, 1200 s, the kernel silent -- a `def` cell that\nthe kernel never answered because something the previous cell left running\nstarved its event loop. Nobody has seen the kernel''s stack at that moment, and\nan equivalent environment did not reproduce it locally. The kernels nbconvert\nlaunches now run `scripts/nbconvert_kernel_watchdog.py` as an IPython startup\nfile (`IPYTHONDIR`, set by the `nbconvert--` task): `faulthandler` dumps every\nthread''s stack to the kernel''s original stderr after 900 s, which ipykernel\nforwards to the job log. It needs neither the GIL nor the event loop, so a\nbusy loop cannot hide from it; healthy kernels exit in seconds and never\nreach it. Checked with a 0.5 s timer: the dump lands in nbconvert''s stderr,\nnot in any cell output, and conversion still succeeds.\n\nAlso fixes a pre-existing race in `test_schedule_run_from_another_loop_hands_over`\n(it failed on windows/py3.10 in this PR''s CI and passed on retry): the test\nreleased the parked runs as soon as the old runner was cancelled, but the new\nrunner may not have parked yet, and a run that parks after `release` waits\nforever. The poll now also waits for the new run to have started.","tree":{"sha":"5416d76a67b69f5ce2f378e1c1c9375ce83011b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/git/trees/5416d76a67b69f5ce2f378e1c1c9375ce83011b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/git/commits/00f48e1f59dec2009fa3fc47e5fda5fdd15dba49","verification":{"payload":"tree 5416d76a67b6