b.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commits/00f48e1f59dec2009fa3fc47e5fda5fdd15dba49"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6493354?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dfreeman06","id":6493354,"login":"dfreeman06","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0OTMzNTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dfreeman06","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/commits/2165b9703948746e62ad313ab4b5e03a473f495f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T01:23:16Z","email":"freeman.dane@gmail.com","name":"dfreeman06"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T01:23:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Stop leaking widgets on every refresh (#179)\n\n* Stop leaking widgets on every refresh (#176)\n\nPipeStatus is now a frozen dataclass instead of a Widget, so a status\nchange no longer opens a comm that is never closed. Instances compare by\nidentity, so assigning a new status still notifies `status` observers.\n\nPipelineStatusView builds its rows once per set of sub-pipes and closes\nthe rows (and their layouts/styles) it replaces, never the sub-pipes'' own\nstatus views; its header HBox is built once too.\n\nscripts/bench_pipeline.py gains a `Comm opens` column.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Gate CI on the pipeline benchmark''s deterministic counts\n\n`pixi run bench-check` runs scripts/bench_pipeline.py headlessly (flat\nand nested 100-node graphs, plus a slow-browser run) and compares comm\nopens, messages and bytes in both directions, layout runs, layouts and\nerrors to scripts/bench_baseline.json. Counts are deterministic run to\nrun, so they must match exactly: a rise is a regression and a fall must\nbe locked in with `pixi run bench-update`, so every cost change is a\nreviewed baseline diff. The slow-browser run gates only layouts and\nerrors, since its resend counts depend on timing. Timings go to the job\nsummary and are never gated.\n\nAgainst master''s unfixed src/ the gate reports the #176 leak as 18\nregressions (comm opens 0 -> 12-14 per phase).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Address review: 8.0.x registry, empty and swapped status views, gate shape\n\n- The leak tests read `Widget.widgets` on ipywidgets 8.0.x, which has no\n  such attribute; use `Widget._active_widgets` there (`_instances` on 8.1+).\n- An empty pipeline''s status view rendered nothing: the row cache matched\n  `()` on the first update and the header was never placed.\n- Rows and the header went stale when a sub-pipe''s `status_widget` or the\n  view''s `html` was replaced: the row cache is keyed on (pipe, view) pairs\n  and the header''s children are set on every update.\n- The view tracks the widgets it creates and closes those, instead of\n  unpacking each row''s children.\n- Tests now pin row reuse by identity, closing every part of a stale row,\n  the collapse toggle, the empty pipeline and swapped views; each mutant\n  the review found survives no longer.\n- bench_check: a phase the benchmark could not complete is gated as\n  `failed` instead of crashing, and `errors` is gated only where the\n  benchmark records it (burst). The CI step runs after the acceptance\n  tests so a baseline change cannot skip them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Replace PipelineStatusView.statuses with a private row list\n\n`statuses` held the view''s row HBoxes, not statuses, and was a traitlet\nonly so `_update_children` could observe it. It was never synced: the\nview is a stock VBox and the rows reach the frontend as `children`. Now\nthat `update_children` places the rows itself, the trait and its\nobserver add nothing, so the rows live in a private `_rows` list and\nonly `collapsed` is observed. The rendered children are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dane <dane@Mac-Box.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d3ef74f880fa8e121f84bb84f21b5c23598ee613","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/git/trees/d3ef74f880fa8e121f84bb84f21b5c23598ee613"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jupyrdf/ipyelk/git/commits/2165b9703948746e62ad313ab4b5e03a473f495f","verification":{"payload":"tree d3ef74f880fa8e121f84bb84f21b5c23598ee613\nparent ad904ce5717036950f3c497a40b5f3b83163a9dd\nauthor dfreeman06 <freeman.dane@gmail.com> 1790817796 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790817796 -0400\n\nStop leaking widgets on every refresh (#179)\n\n* Stop leaking widgets on every refresh (#176)\n\nPipeStatus is now a frozen dataclass instead of a Widget, so a status\nchange no longer opens a comm that is never closed. Instances compare by\nidentity, so assigning a new status still notifies `status` observers.\n\nPipelineStatusView builds its rows once per set of sub-pipes and closes\nthe rows (and their layouts/styles) it replaces, never the sub-pipes'' own\nstatus views; its header HBox is built once too.\n\nscripts/bench_pipeline.py gains a `Comm opens` column.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Gate CI on the pipeline benchmark''s deterministic counts\n\n`pixi run bench-check` runs scripts/bench_pipeline.py headlessly (flat\nand nested 100-node graphs, plus a slow-browser run) and compares comm\nopens, messages and bytes in both directions, layout runs, layouts and\nerrors to scripts/bench_baseline.json. Counts are deterministic run to\nrun, so they must match exactly: a rise is a regression and a fall must\nbe locked in with `pixi run bench-update`, so every cost change is a\nreviewed baseline diff. The slow-browser run gates only layouts and\nerrors, since its resend counts depend on timing. Timings go to the job\nsummary and are never gated.\n\nAgainst master''s unfixed src/ the gate reports the #176 leak as 18\nregressions (comm opens 0 -> 12-14 per phase).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Address review: 8.0.x registry, empty and swapped status views, gate shape\n\n- The leak tests read `Widget.widgets` on ipywidgets 8.0.x, which has no\n  such attribute; use `Widget._active_widgets` there (`_instances` on 8.1+).\n- An empty pipeline''s status view rendered nothing: the row cache matched\n  `()` on the first update and the header was never placed.\n- Rows and the header went stale when a sub-pipe''s `status_widget` or the\n  view''s `html` was replaced: the row cache is keyed on (pipe, view) pairs\n  and the header''s children are set on every update.\n- The view tracks the widgets it creates and closes those, instead of\n  unpacking each row''s children.\n- Tests now pin row reuse by identity, closing every part of a stale row,\n  the collapse toggle, the empty pipeline and swapped views; each mutant\n  the review found survives no longer.\n- bench_check: a phase the benchmark could not complete is gated as\n  `failed` instead of crashing, and `errors` is gated only where the\n  benchmark records it (burst). The CI step runs after the acceptance\n  tests so a baseline change cannot skip them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n* Replace PipelineStatusView.statuses with a private row list\n\n`statuses` held the view''s row HBoxes, not statuses, and was a traitlet\nonly so `_update_children` could observe it. It was never synced: the\nview is a stock VBox and the rows reach the frontend as `children`. Now\nthat `update_children` places the rows itself, the trait and its\nobserver add nothing, so the rows live in a private `_rows` list and\nonly `collapsed` is observed. The rendered children are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011vSpw2xTz8xqJoCPBrd7kw\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dane <dane@Mac-Box.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvbYECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyA4QACykrskrKqQqZwni0EW/IkBq\nQOnL/aPqiLO0IzPQs3hS1Vbhx1CLBZntnspUVJ2NqCP2vPVyvPC+tV2764NgN36E\nCxxItis9QkdKgVtgpECgXleAyoDsk1oy89a5UqmgfOQ7oeDMB7GDhJqLY+730MlT\nz7JVi917z2NdRcgBAlWvuXAEfz1a8jeiKnQUP4RGUBWHV+Z4cHRNk/xW8D9YDOX2\nkGr1kWRRdADj27BKUDsPzzQjk+9+OIikXBlQZ46fZBMaManq5WBGHAQTjvKS35Xu\n6esc2K5DGFsIQJhSsNH1x5ezDC/s30zywfwpJ3khT+78qbztb2OOVOAUh6Y2hR3S\nuF5rK8rSc+gsnJGImZF59bZNDgimxg3RSkZonwHpBVyRZ4VmGWRuKCoJrHNlzN2g\n40Ryt5FCORXC51USUWCtm6AdzEimoGrZQZ33m42xMi1ybbBLmjcuiRyxnfZOBIuI\nQKrpO6Kn3efENTbvP4tmml/0eS7AEr2eJlkWhJTJN5cZXcBVQPZazg05Y0SWMPV5\nWoM3pN/WWmWTPF0Tz0witj72TMC+gqDs+k8UCJc+r9j+j3TCN6/YuA+fsd4Blvtp\nSayR